KustoLoco.Geo
=============

This package EMBEDS a default geo database so geo_info_from_ip_address() works out of
the box: DB-IP "IP to Country Lite" joined with Google canonical country centroids.
It can also read a geo-IP dataset you supply at runtime (e.g. the DB-IP "IP to City
Lite" database) when city/state precision or IPv6 coverage is needed.

The DB-IP Lite databases are made available by DB-IP (https://db-ip.com) under the
Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License (CC-BY-4.0).

If you distribute an application that uses a DB-IP Lite dataset with this provider,
you must attribute DB-IP, for example:

    IP Geolocation by DB-IP (https://db-ip.com)

See https://db-ip.com/db/lite.php for the current license terms.

The per-country coordinates in the embedded dataset are the Google canonical country
centroids (https://github.com/google/dspl/blob/master/samples/google/canonical/countries.csv),
(C) Google, likewise licensed CC-BY-4.0. Redistributing the embedded dataset therefore
carries BOTH attributions:

    IP Geolocation by DB-IP (https://db-ip.com)
    Country centroids (C) Google (https://github.com/google/dspl), CC-BY-4.0

Because this package ships that dataset inside the assembly, an application that merely
depends on the package is redistributing it — carry the two lines above in your own
third-party notices.

This provider reads any of the DB-IP Lite layouts — City Lite
(ip_start, ip_end, continent, country, stateprov, city, latitude, longitude), Country
Lite (ip_start, ip_end, country), or a compact country+centroid derivation
(ip_start, ip_end, country, latitude, longitude) — and any CSV using one of those column
layouts; if you use a different source, follow that source's own attribution requirements.
